**Status**: DRAFT for review (David 2026-07-18). The runtime half of the HA/ESPHome story (the design-time half is mining, [CXC-HALD-MINE]). A ComposeBus `adaptor` peer that bridges a LIVE HA instance bidirectionally — HA entities → by-quantity namespaces ([CXC-HAB-INGRESS]), ComposeBus commands → HA service calls ([CXC-HAB-EGRESS]) — over a declarative default-deny map ([CXC-HAB-MAPPING]), as a graceful-if-absent adaptor app ([CXC-HAB-ADAPTOR]) with authority-gated egress ([CXC-HAB-AUTHORITY]). Demotes the hub to a peer; runs NO HA plugin code in any mode.

**Architect — build plan flagged for David's go-ahead (NOT started):** (1) the `ha` adaptor app (host ComposeApp; MQTT `statestream` subscribe + optional WebSocket) — mirror `composeio.adaptors.wled` at instance scale; (2) the ingress mapper (HA domain/attrs → by-quantity namespaces) + auto-suggest from the entity registry; (3) the egress mapper (command namespace → service call) + authority-gate; (4) the declarative default-deny map + `transform`. Suggested first slice: subscribe a mock HA `statestream`, bridge one `sensor.*` → `env/temperature` and one `light.*` round-trip, all against a mocked HA — proving both directions + graceful-absence with no real HA.

**Architect — ratifications flagged:** (1) new node-prefix `CXC-HAB-` (HA-Bridge), a `CXC-` sub-family — needs a [CONV-PREFIX] row. (2) whether the `bridge`/`ha` adaptor is a new entry in [CXC-HALD-KINDS]'s `adaptor` family (I have it so) or its own family. (3) transport choice: HA MQTT `statestream` (simplest, needs the HA MQTT integration enabled) vs the WebSocket API (no MQTT dependency, richer) — recommend MQTT-first, WebSocket as an option. (4) the entity→namespace auto-suggest table (HA domain → default quantity) should share the CONVENTION registry proposed for [CXC-HALD-NAMESPACE].
